From f99e10fec99c5d67c8526bce4543c69a415f133b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kudriavuy <169286443+kudriavuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:19:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Emoji panel

Command = "Emoji" opens a panel over the program's part of the row: a
close button, a category key and one row of all emoji (Unicode's
emoji-test.txt, no skin tones; recently used first) that scrolls with
the finger and runs on after a flick. A tapped emoji goes to the helper
("emoji <text>"), which puts it on the clipboard and reports it in
.../paste; tiny-dfr then presses Ctrl+V (Ctrl+Shift+V in the programs of
EmojiPasteShift). Glyphs are drawn once by Pango (pangocairo: sequences,
flags, colour) and kept; EmojiFont picks the font.

Upstream: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/tiny-dfr (applies to 285faff8b8cae893e9babd673b904929dd6f7f9c)
